Create a Java program that asks the user for:

Student's age
Quiz score
Attendance percentage
Conditions:

A student is eligible to take the final exam if:

Age is 18 or above AND
Quiz score is 50 or above AND
Attendance is 75% or above

If all conditions are true, display:

Eligible for Final Exam

Otherwise, display:

Not Eligible for Final Exam



SOURCE CODE

import java.util.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

     System.out.print("age ");
     int age = sc.nextInt();
     
     System.out.print("quiz score ");
     int score = sc.nextInt();
     
     sc.nextLine();
     
     System.out.print("attendance percentage ");
     int atDance = sc.nextInt(); 

     if ( age >= 18 && score >= 50 && atDance >= 75) {
         
        System.out.println("Qualified!");
         
     } else
      
      System.out.println("Not Qualified");

    }
}
